#: includes/checks/class-checks-security.php:139
msgid "Site is not configured for HTTPS — Site Address uses an http scheme."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-checks-security.php:140
msgid "Install an SSL certificate (most hosts offer free Let's Encrypt). Then go to Settings → General and update both Site URL and Home URL to https://. Update any hardcoded http URLs in content via a search-replace tool such as WP-CLI's `wp search-replace`."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-checks-security.php:162
msgid "readme.html exists in the WordPress root. PreFlight cannot verify HTTP accessibility without loopback (Phase 5); this file exposes the WordPress version to anyone who fetches it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-checks-security.php:163
msgid "Delete readme.html from the WordPress root, or block public access at the server level (e.g., an Nginx location block or .htaccess deny rule)."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: comma-separated list of found backup filenames
#: includes/checks/class-checks-security.php:192
#, php-format
msgid "Backup or temporary copies of wp-config.php exist in the WordPress root: %s. These may expose database credentials if HTTP-accessible."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-checks-security.php:195
msgid "Delete the listed files, or move them outside the webroot. Never leave wp-config backups in a publicly-served directory."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-checks-security.php:218
msgid "XML-RPC is enabled. While not inherently a vulnerability, XML-RPC has historically been used for brute-force and DDoS amplification."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-checks-security.php:219
msgid "If the site does not use XML-RPC (Jetpack, WordPress mobile apps, some IFTTT recipes, third-party publishing tools), disable it via a plugin or via `add_filter('xmlrpc_enabled', '__return_false');` in a small mu-plugin."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-checks-security.php:238
msgid "WordPress allows in-dashboard editing of theme and plugin files. An admin account with edit permissions can modify executable PHP files directly through the admin UI."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-checks-security.php:239
msgid "In wp-config.php, add: define('DISALLOW_FILE_EDIT', true); — this disables the Theme and Plugin file editors."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-checks-security.php:262
msgid "Database table prefix is the default wp_. Changing it is a minor obscurity step against generic SQL injection attempts that hardcode wp_ table names."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-checks-security.php:263
msgid "Changing the prefix on an existing install requires renaming tables and updating wp-config.php and a few serialized option keys. Best done at install time. If migrating, use WP-CLI or a dedicated plugin and verify nothing breaks before completing the launch."
msgstr ""

